  "documentation": {
    "range": "The species' native range is the Amazon, Orinoco and Oyapock river basin, and it is introduced elsewhere in southern Florida and Puerto Rico.",
    "population": "<p>There are no data on population size and trends for this species, but it is very common and abundant.</p>",
    "habitats": "<span>The species preferably inhabits quiet shallow waters in mud-bottomed and sand-bottomed rivers and ponds.   It feeds on small fish, crayfish, worms and insect larvae (Froese and Pauly 2019).",
    "threats": "<p>There is no information about threats to this species.</p>",
    "measures": "<p>There is no information on conservation actions in place or recommended for this species.</p>",
    "use_trade": "The species is used in the aquarium and food trade.",
    "rationale": "<p>Despite there being little information available on this species, it has a wide range, which is unlikely to have severe threats. It is therefore assessed as Least Concern.</p>",
